        @akr.work.authoring-contracts,
        @akr.work.revise-lifecycle-semantics, and
        @akr.work.reference-supersession-consistency.

        REPORT-BY-REPORT DISPOSITION (in collation order):
        1 scope term containing a rendered `path` prefix — live, authoring-contracts;
        2 explain AKR-X099 — crash resolved, valid-slot feedback remains authoring-contracts;
        3 write leaves lock stale — CLI remedy resolved, MCP remedy remains authoring-contracts;
        4 Lege transport closure plus explain identifier mismatch — transport-reliability and authoring-contracts;
        5 papercut namespace retry — resolved by schema and CLI help;
        6 ready-to-active revise created proposed head — live, revise-lifecycle-semantics;
        7 per-kind slots/relations and commit type retries — live, authoring-contracts;
        8 pinned context goal rejected — live, reference-supersession-consistency;
        9 different-key supersession rejected — live, reference-supersession-consistency;
        10 active decision content revision became proposed — live, revise-lifecycle-semantics;
        11 SaveYourSkin repeated transport closure — live, transport-reliability;
        12 observation observed_at type omitted — live, authoring-contracts;
        13 verified observation provenance/command mismatch — live, authoring-contracts;
        14 assessment as_of type omitted — live, authoring-contracts;
        15 propose --from body shape misleading — live, authoring-contracts;
        16 raw-autotune explain/papercut transport closure — live, transport-reliability;
        17 CLI/MCP search argument mismatch — live low-severity, authoring-contracts;
        18 raw-autotune context transport closure — live, transport-reliability.
        """
    confidence high
    as_of git:ff0170d6ffe2f5b1d55eb63f6c8ae469bd36cff6
    derived_from [
        @akr.papercut.collated-18-papercuts-from-evidence-intake/1,
